# PR Plan Trigger

When the user starts implementing a ticket or asks how to split work across PRs:

1. If the ticket's `## PR Plan` section is empty, missing, or stale, always read and follow `.cursor/skills/layered-pr-planner/SKILL.md` before writing code.
2. The skill produces a per-layer PR plan with stack rationale when the estimated implementation lines exceed ~400.
3. The plan is appended to the ticket in append-only fashion.

An empty, missing, or stale `## PR Plan` is resolved by this trigger; it is not a permanent blocker once the layered plan is appended to the ticket.

Layer order for contract changes (adapt to your project's architecture):

```
domain -> data-access -> functions -> infrastructure -> feature -> experience
```

Pair with `.cursor/rules/process/one-layer-per-pr.mdc` and `.cursor/rules/process/pr-size-and-stack.mdc`.
